steps.text:
Average power is a poor summary of a ride that keeps changing: it can't show how the power was spread or how much metabolic stress it caused [[c:avg-hides]].

[Normalised power](g:normalised-power) (NP) tries to fix that in four steps [[c:np-algorithm]]:

1. take 30-s rolling averages of power;
2. raise each to the 4th power;
3. average those;
4. take the 4th root.

The 30-s smoothing is meant to follow the body's delayed response to a change in power, and the 4th power its curved, faster-than-linear rise in strain [[c:np-rationale]]. So a criterium full of surges gets an NP well above its average power; a steady time trial gets an NP close to its average.
